{"id": "s01u000001", "type": "statement", "text": "LiteLLM exposes /v1/messages and an Anthropic-format SDK entry point for non-Anthropic providers; endpoint availability does not imply lossless Anthropic feature parity.", "source_url": "https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/anthropic_unified", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "/v1/messages", "Anthropic", "LiteLLM", "Messages"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 3.4, "also": ["https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/anthropic_unified/native_passthrough"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000002", "type": "fact", "text": "The Chat bridge maps client-tool input_schema into OpenAI function parameters; the schema describes arguments, while tool execution stays with the client application.", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/82d8b3797cf124e2baaa9c342f87a57fbb3a1a96/litellm/llms/anthropic/pass_through/adapters/transformation.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "Chat", "input_schema", "tool"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 2.4, "also": ["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/handle-tool-calls"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000003", "type": "fact", "text": "The Chat bridge maps assistant tool_use blocks to function tool_calls and user tool_result blocks to role=tool messages, preserving call/result correlation through id and tool_call_id.", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/82d8b3797cf124e2baaa9c342f87a57fbb3a1a96/litellm/llms/anthropic/pass_through/adapters/transformation.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "Chat", "Messages", "tool", "tool_call_id", "tool_calls", "tool_result", "tool_use"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 5.6, "also": ["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/handle-tool-calls"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000004", "type": "fact", "text": "On the Chat return path, LiteLLM reconstructs tool_use blocks from structured tool_calls and maps finish_reason=tool_calls to stop_reason=tool_use.", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/82d8b3797cf124e2baaa9c342f87a57fbb3a1a96/litellm/llms/anthropic/pass_through/adapters/transformation.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "Chat", "LiteLLM", "finish_reason", "stop_reason", "tool_calls", "tool_use"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 5.0, "also": ["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/handle-tool-calls"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000010", "type": "fact", "text": "For client function tools, the application executes each selected call and returns its result; generating a tool block does not perform the operation.", "source_url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/handle-tool-calls", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "function-tool", "tool"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.6, "also": ["https://docs.ollama.com/capabilities/tool-calling", "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/features/tool_calling/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000006", "type": "statement", "text": "The Chat adapter maps Anthropic tool_choice any to required, auto to auto, tool to a named function, and none to none; downstream support remains a separate check.", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/82d8b3797cf124e2baaa9c342f87a57fbb3a1a96/litellm/llms/anthropic/pass_through/adapters/transformation.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "Anthropic", "Chat", "tool", "tool_choice"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "parameters", "relation": "about", "score": 3.2, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000007", "type": "statement", "text": "At the inspected commit, openai/ Messages requests use Responses by default. For a chat-only target, use_chat_completions_url_for_anthropic_messages selects the Chat bridge instead.", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/82d8b3797cf124e2baaa9c342f87a57fbb3a1a96/litellm/llms/anthropic/pass_through/messages/handler.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "Chat", "Messages", "Responses", "use_chat_completions_url_for_anthropic_messages"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "parameters", "relation": "about", "score": 3.2, "also": ["https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/proxy/config_settings"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000008", "type": "statement", "text": "If the upstream implements Messages natively, model_info.supported_endpoints can opt into /v1/messages passthrough; ordinary OpenAI compatibility alone is insufficient for that opt-in.", "source_url": "https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/anthropic_unified/native_passthrough", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "/v1/messages", "Messages", "passthrough", "supported_endpoints"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "parameters", "relation": "about", "score": 3.2, "also": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/82d8b3797cf124e2baaa9c342f87a57fbb3a1a96/litellm/llms/anthropic/pass_through/messages/handler.py"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000005", "type": "fact", "text": "LiteLLM's Chat-stream wrapper emits Anthropic block lifecycle events and input_json_delta fragments. Clients must assemble tool arguments by block and wait for closure before parsing them.", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/82d8b3797cf124e2baaa9c342f87a57fbb3a1a96/litellm/llms/anthropic/pass_through/adapters/streaming_iterator.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "Anthropic", "LiteLLM", "input_json_delta", "tool"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "how-to", "relation": "about", "score": 3.4, "also": ["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/messages-streaming"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000011", "type": "fact", "text": "Verify native function-tool capability and model-specific parsing before using a translated local backend for agent work; an API wrapper cannot supply missing model competence.", "source_url": "https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers/ollama", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "function-tool"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "how-to", "relation": "about", "score": 0.8, "also": ["https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/features/tool_calling/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000012", "type": "fact", "text": "Treat initial HTTP 200 as provisional for streamed generation: Anthropic errors can arrive in SSE after headers, and LiteLLM's Messages router explicitly handles stream error events.", "source_url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/errors", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "Anthropic", "HTTP 200", "LiteLLM", "Messages", "stream"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 4.2, "also": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/82d8b3797cf124e2baaa9c342f87a57fbb3a1a96/litellm/router.py"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
{"id": "s01u000009", "type": "statement", "text": "Translation can approximate or lose Anthropic-only details. Native passthrough also reduces cache_control to its portable core unless cache_control_ttl is enabled; avoid promising byte-for-byte fidelity.", "source_url": "https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/anthropic_unified/native_passthrough", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["LiteLLM Anthropic Messages interoperability", "cache_control_ttl", "passthrough"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.6, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword"}
